{"name":"Fairy Salt","hex":"#ffe0f5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical being of human form with magical powers, known in many sizes and descriptions, although typically depicted as a small sprite with gauze-like wings, especially one that is female. Fairies are revered in some modern forms of paganism.","A male homosexual, especially one who is effeminate."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Like a fairy; fanciful, whimsical, delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy"},{"term":"salt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common substance, chemically consisting mainly of sodium chloride (NaCl), used extensively as a food ingredient, seasoning, condiment, and preservative.","One of the compounds formed from the reaction of an acid with a base, where a positive ion replaces a hydrogen of the acid."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of water: containing salt, saline.","Treated with salt as a preservative; cured with salt, salted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy","wikidata":"Q8028"},{"title":"Salt","blocks":[{"text":"Salt is a mineral composed primarily of sodium chloride (NaCl). When used in food, especially in granulated form, it is more formally called table salt. In the form of a natural crystalline mineral, salt is also known as rock salt or halite. Salt is essential for life in general, and saltiness is one of the basic human tastes. Salt is one of the oldest and most ubiquitous food seasonings, and is known to uniformly improve the taste perception of food. Salting, brining, and pickling are ancient and important methods of food preservation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Rock_salt_%28halitite%29_%28Billianwala_Salt_Member%2C_Salt_Range_Formation%2C_Ediacaran_to_Lower_Cambrian%3B_Khewra_Salt_Mine%2C_Salt_Range%2C_Pakistan%29_14.jpg/330px-Rock_salt_%28halitite%29_%28Billianwala_Salt_Member%2C_Salt_Range_Formation%2C_Ediacaran_to_Lower_Cambrian%3B_Khewra_Salt_Mine%2C_Salt_Range%2C_Pakistan%29_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt","wikidata":"Q11254"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg/500px-James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg/1280px-James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg/500px-James_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Title page of a 1603 reprinting of Daemonologie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_I%3B_Daemonologie%2C_in_forme_of_a_dialogue._Title_page._Wellcome_M0014280.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki